WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.652
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:16.714
Unit one: Tenses Review: Present, Past and Future. Today you will choose the correct tense for time and meaning.

4
00:00:17.014 --> 00:00:19.748
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.026
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.699
Habit.

7
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:28.834
Habit means something you do regularly.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.985
Reading is a good habit.

9
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:34.038
Your turn. Say: Habit.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.611
Habit.

11
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.142
Permanent.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.521
Permanent means lasting for a long time.

13
00:00:43.117 --> 00:00:44.861
This is a permanent job.

14
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.731
Your turn. Say: Permanent.

15
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:51.475
Permanent.

16
00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:53.299
Temporary.

17
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:56.620
Temporary means lasting a short time.

18
00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:58.984
It is a temporary change.

19
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:02.421
Your turn. Say: Temporary.

20
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.326
Temporary.

21
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:07.957
Schedule.

22
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.147
Schedule means a planned timetable.

23
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.564
The train schedule changed.

24
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.582
Your turn. Say: Schedule.

25
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:20.446
Schedule.

26
00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:22.103
Prediction.

27
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:25.302
Prediction means a guess about the future.

28
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:27.440
That is only a prediction.

29
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.772
Your turn. Say: Prediction.

30
00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:34.553
Prediction.

31
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:36.376
Interrupt.

32
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:39.545
Interrupt means to stop an action.

33
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.755
The phone interrupted me.

34
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.596
Your turn. Say: Interrupt.

35
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:48.458
Interrupt.

36
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:50.404
Sequence.

37
00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:53.648
Sequence means the order of events.

38
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.681
Follow the sequence.

39
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.808
Your turn. Say: Sequence.

40
00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:02.517
Sequence.

41
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:04.389
Contrast.

42
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:07.511
Contrast means a clear difference.

43
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:09.629
There is a contrast here.

44
00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:12.683
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

45
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:16.581
Contrast.

46
00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:21.180
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:25.328
Visal, which tense do I use for habits and facts?

48
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:36.964
Use the present simple for habits and facts, such as She walks to school. Use the present continuous for actions happening now or temporary situations.

49
00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.376
And for the past?

50
00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:53.489
Use the past simple for finished actions and the past continuous for an action in progress when another action interrupted it, such as I was reading when the lights went out.

51
00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:56.409
How do I talk about the future?

52
00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:08.749
Use will for predictions and quick decisions, be going to for plans, and the present continuous for fixed arrangements. Always check the time words in the sentence.

53
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.273
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:15.045
Grammar focus: Choosing the right tense.

55
00:03:15.345 --> 00:03:16.578
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:19.225
She walks to school every day.

57
00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:22.267
I was reading when the lights went out.

58
00:03:23.233 --> 00:03:31.502
Match the tense to the time word: every day uses the present simple, yesterday uses the past simple and tomorrow often uses will or going to.

59
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.052
Be careful! Don't say: I am go to school every day.

60
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.394
Say: I go to school every day.

61
00:03:40.694 --> 00:03:42.729
Habit: present simple.

62
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:46.325
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.216
A Busy Week.

64
00:03:48.516 --> 00:03:51.061
Sophea walks to school every day.

65
00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:54.740
Yesterday she was studying when the power went out.

66
00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:58.348
Right now she is revising for her exam.

67
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.461
Tomorrow she is going to visit her cousin.

68
00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.350
She thinks it will rain in the evening.

69
00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:09.445
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.434
Every day uses the present blank.

71
00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:16.109
A, future. B, simple. C, perfect.

72
00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.875
The answer is B: simple.

73
00:04:23.017 --> 00:04:24.505
I blank when the phone rang.

74
00:04:24.805 --> 00:04:28.319
A, cook. B, will cook. C, was cooking.

75
00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:33.982
The answer is C: was cooking.

76
00:04:35.117 --> 00:04:37.116
A plan uses be going blank.

77
00:04:37.416 --> 00:04:40.141
A, to. B, at. C, for.

78
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.398
The answer is A: to.

79
00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.584
Yesterday uses the past blank.

80
00:04:48.884 --> 00:04:52.271
A, base. B, simple. C, future.

81
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:57.694
The answer is B: simple.

82
00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.455
What is Sophea doing now?

83
00:05:00.755 --> 00:05:04.455
A, sleeping. B, travelling. C, revising.

84
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.348
The answer is C: revising.

85
00:05:11.533 --> 00:05:14.662
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:15.517 --> 00:05:17.679
Which tense do you use for a plan?

87
00:05:26.483 --> 00:05:28.077
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.377 --> 00:05:39.356
I use be going to for a plan I have already made, such as I am going to study tonight. I use will for a prediction or a quick decision. I check the time words in the sentence.

89
00:05:39.656 --> 00:05:41.504
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:42.417 --> 00:05:46.613
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and choosing the right tense.

91
00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:52.294
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:05:52.594 --> 00:05:55.072
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:05:55.372 --> 00:05:59.069
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

